%% Two conventions matter for this bibliography style:
%%  1. oup-abbrvnat applies BibTeX's "t" case change, which lowercases every
%%     title word that is not brace-protected. All acronyms are therefore
%%     wrapped in braces -- {HLA}, {TCR}, {MHC}, {NLP} and so on. Do not strip
%%     those braces.
%%  2. The file is deliberately pure ASCII: the document class loads no
%%     inputenc/fontenc, so accents are written as LaTeX escapes
%%     (T{\"u}reci, Mart{\'i}nez) rather than as UTF-8 bytes.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

